            'blocks'  => [
                [ 'p', 'A sticker printer and cutter doesn’t have to use a blade. The xTool M2 with its CMYK inkjet module prints a full-colour design and then laser-cuts its outline, while two cameras with live preview help line the cut up with the print. A classic blade cutting plotter is still the right tool for lettering and decals made from PVC vinyl, which must never be laser cut, but on its own it neither prints nor engraves.' ],
                [ 'p', 'Below we explain how printing and cutting stickers works on the M2, how this print and cut machine differs from a blade plotter, which sticker materials are laser-safe and which must never go under a laser, and which module and fume extraction to choose.' ],
                [ 'h2', 'How does print and cut work on the xTool M2?' ],
                [ 'p', 'The xTool M2 is an enclosed craft machine that, according to xTool, prints, cuts and engraves a wide range of materials. It comes with a 10, 20 or 40 W laser. Printing is handled by the CMYK inkjet module, sold separately or in the Color Print & Cut bundle. A sticker sheet takes a few steps:' ],
