                [ 'h2', 'Which sticker materials can you laser cut – and which never?' ],
                [ 'p', 'The most important rule: never cut or engrave PVC (polyvinyl chloride) with a laser. In the beam it breaks down and releases chlorine compounds, mainly hydrogen chloride. This irritates the airways and, with moisture, forms hydrochloric acid that corrodes the machine. The catch is that many self-adhesive films sold as “vinyl” are exactly that: PVC.' ],
